    },
    {
      "id": "KeYW-ebSeQFjE7FIzJRsN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8779.108523588502,
      "y": 774.2597661773625,
      "width": 307.2998046875,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBC",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1234716192,
      "version": 356,
      "versionNonce": 799589344,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789647160413,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "My understood about it (pt-br)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "My understood about it (pt-br)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "jrgYYxf3IFL7RkDfio_jh",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9248.895197272743,
      "y": 822.8015309201874,
      "width": 467.8943775504262,
      "height": 279.5875857918406,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 384467488,
      "version": 1640,
      "versionNonce": 1056653280,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789657064008,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Em termos práticos: se uma classe filha precisa lançar\nUnsupportedOperationException, ignora métodos herdados ou altera resultados\nesperados, provavelmente a hierarquia está mal modelada.\n\nEsse será o exemplo que abordo aqui mais a frente!\n\nConta bancária (cenário)\n\nEste exemplo é bastante intuitivo: uma conta comum permite saque, mas uma conta\nde investimento pode não permitir retirada imediata. Fazer InvestmentAccount herdar\nde uma conta cujo contrato promete saque viola a LSP.\n\nA solução é separar contratos por capacidade: toda conta pode consultar saldo, mas\napenas contas sacáveis devem implementar a operação de saque.\n\nA conta de investimento nem pode ser enviada acidentalmente para esse serviço, pois\nela não implementa WithdrawableAccount.\n\nUltimately, what is really worth remembering is: \"A derived class can be substituted\nfor its base class.\"",
      "fontSize": 11.183503431673623,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Em termos práticos: se uma classe filha precisa lançar UnsupportedOperationException, ignora métodos herdados ou altera resultados esperados, provavelmente a hierarquia está mal modelada.\n\nEsse será o exemplo que abordo aqui mais a frente!\n\nConta bancária (cenário)\n\nEste exemplo é bastante intuitivo: uma conta comum permite saque, mas uma conta de investimento pode não permitir retirada imediata. Fazer InvestmentAccount herdar de uma conta cujo contrato promete saque viola a LSP.\n\nA solução é separar contratos por capacidade: toda conta pode consultar saldo, mas apenas contas sacáveis devem implementar a operação de saque.\n\nA conta de investimento nem pode ser enviada acidentalmente para esse serviço, pois ela não implementa WithdrawableAccount.\n\nUltimately, what is really worth remembering is: \"A derived class can be substituted for its base class.\"",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "shyj44mvY9TJ5H1UKRgWf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9867.196197777526,
      "y": 823.85216781191,
      "width": 429.6664149821925,
      "height": 237.64944792306449,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBE",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1989492256,
      "version": 1549,
      "versionNonce": 727541280,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789649726749,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This principle dictates that any subclass must be able to replace its base\nclass without breaking expected behavior.\n\nThe subclass must adhere to the behavioral contract defined by the\nabstraction.\n\nThe return type of a subclass method must match or be a subtype of the\nreturn type of the superclass method. If the base method is of type\n`Account`, you inherit the `Account` interface down to your service; for\ninstance, you wouldn't create an `AccountPCD` directly without it inheriting\nfrom `Account` in some way!\n\nThe Liskov Substitution Principle also addresses scenarios where inherited\nbehavior—which shouldn't occur in the new service—forces you to execute it\nanyway!\n\n",
      "fontSize": 11.183503431673623,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This principle dictates that any subclass must be able to replace its base class without breaking expected behavior.\n\nThe subclass must adhere to the behavioral contract defined by the abstraction.\n\nThe return type of a subclass method must match or be a subtype of the return type of the superclass method. If the base method is of type `Account`, you inherit the `Account` interface down to your service; for instance, you wouldn't create an `AccountPCD` directly without it inheriting from `Account` in some way!\n\nThe Liskov Substitution Principle also addresses scenarios where inherited behavior—which shouldn't occur in the new service—forces you to execute it anyway!\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "316qmgQ9yr97kucSZyuQy",
